BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTSTAMP:20261012T091551Z
SUMMARY:Very easy recovery
DESCRIPTION:Week 1 (RECOVERY FROM HM). Planned distance: 10 km. Weekly plan
 ned distance: 42 km.\n\n10 km very easy.\nOptional 4 x 20 s relaxed stride
 s only if legs feel completely normal.\n\nEasy running: conversational and
  relaxed\, with no pace target. HR may often be around 130-150 bpm but the
 re is no minimum HR\; do not speed up to raise HR or force Apple Watch Zon
 e 2.\nStrides: 4-6 x 20 s unless specified otherwise\, fast but relaxed wi
 th full recovery and good mechanics\; never all-out sprinting. Keep them l
 ow fatigue.\n\nBuild weeks maintain the aerobic base while improving speed
  endurance at approximately 56-61 km\, with one major Thursday quality ses
 sion plus strides and selected long-run finishes. Health\, enjoyment and s
 ustainable progression take priority over mileage. If fatigue accumulates\
 , shorten Tuesday first\, then Sunday\; localised pain\, altered gait or w
 orsening soreness calls for reduced load. Optional manually added Saturday
 : 6-10 km very easy\; redistribute mileage by shortening Sunday first\, th
 en Tuesday\, preserving Thursday quality\; do not automatically add volume
  or exceed approximately 60-62 km.\n\nBlock context supplied by athlete: H
 M approximately 1:32 (about 4:22/km)\, previous 50-60 km/week across three
  running days and repeated 24-27 km long runs. Maintain comfortable 20-27
  km endurance\, develop threshold and 5K/10K speed\, and make 4:10-4:20/km
  increasingly sustainable without assuming sub-40 fitness. Final 10K bench
 mark checks progress\; sub-40 is only a stretch goal supported by recent s
 essions. No fourth scheduled running day. Maximal flat-running sprints are
  not added\; optional bike SIT appears only in selected deload description
 s and must not interfere with running quality.\n\nStrength / mobility guid
 ance (no separate gym events):\n\nAssume approximately two gym sessions pe
 r week when recovery permits.\n\nThe athlete also trains upper body for ae
 sthetics and climbing.\n\nNormal gym session may include:\n- pull-ups\n- b
 ench press / chest press\n- DB row / pulley row\n- shoulder press\n- curls
 \n- hanging leg raises\n- optional lateral raises\n- side plank\n\nRunner-
 specific lower-body work:\n- Bulgarian split squat: 2–3 x 6–8/leg\n- R
 omanian deadlift: 2–3 x 6–10\n- calf raises: 2–3 x 10–15\n\nLower-
 body sets should normally stay approximately 2 reps from failure.\n\nThe g
 oal is gradual strength development WITHOUT compromising Thursday quality
  or Sunday long running.\n\nMobility/flexibility may include:\n- 90/90 hip
  rotations\n- World's Greatest Stretch with rotation\n- Cossack lunges\n-
  toe-elevated lunges\n- couch stretch\n\nThe athlete prefers a simple repe
 ated gym routine rather than complicated A/B strength programming.
UID:2026-10-20-tue-d5dd9348-4816-4e9d-ae60-f2341924e651@running-speed-endur
 ance
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
